# What the BRIDGE needs at runtime, and nothing else.
#
# Two direct dependencies. Everything else in the lock is a transitive of
# these two, pinned by `uv pip compile` so a build is reproducible rather
# than "whatever the index served that morning".
#
# INSTALL THE SDK FROM SOURCE, NOT FROM ITS WHEEL. claude-agent-sdk
# publishes one wheel per platform and each carries Claude Code itself as
# package data at claude_agent_sdk/_bundled/claude[.exe] -- 219 MB of the
# SDK's 220. `_find_bundled_cli()` is tried BEFORE shutil.which, so that
# copy is what runs, and nothing we ship can be smaller than it.
#
# The sdist carries no binary (0.3 MB), so `--no-binary claude-agent-sdk`
# gives a pure-Python SDK that falls through to the CLI the user installed.
# That is the shape every artefact now has, and it is why Claude Code is a
# prerequisite rather than cargo.
#
# THE OPTION CANNOT LIVE IN THIS FILE. `uv pip compile` accepts a
# `--no-binary` line here without complaint and silently drops it from the
# output; a lock file has no way to say "take this one from source". So it
# is set where installs actually happen: the user's install line (see
# docs/GUIDE.md) and PIP_NO_BINARY in CI.
claude-agent-sdk==0.2.153

# Lazily imported, in two places: bridge/wire/uiview.py renders the guest's
# UI records to PNG, and bridge/services/attachment.py re-encodes what a
# person drops on the window. Both `from PIL import Image` inside the
# function, so the bridge starts without it and fails at the feature. That
# is not a reason to leave it out of a package.
pillow==12.3.0
